{"t": 1794113010.930962, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "CI is green again. `contract-tests` was failing on `test_fee_rounding_contract`: `fee(2.675)` returned `2.67` instead of `2.68`.\n\nWhat I changed in `payments/fees.py`:\n- Replaced the binary-float rounding with exact decimal arithmetic. The amount is now converted with `Decimal(str(amount))`, the fee math is unchanged, and the result is quantized to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`.\n- This matches the card-network contract in PAY-88 (fees computed on exact decimal values and rounded HALF-UP to cents: `2.675 -> 2.68`, `1.005 -> 1.01`; binary float rounding is explicitly not acceptable there).\n- The signature still takes and returns a `float`, so callers and the rest of the calculation are unaffected.\n\nVerified locally: `fee(2.675) == 2.68`, `fee(1.005) == 1.01`, `fee(100.0) == 100.0`, and the existing test suite passes.", "issue_number": 214, "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
